## Scope

This increment composes the already-proven persisted-`Custom + Validated` universal provenance path into the real `AppServices` graph. It does not add a second profile model, persist universal metadata, infer an original Auto Tuner mode, alter validation/winner authority, or modify WPF presentation.

## Permanent production changes

`src/FFPerformanceEngine.App/AppServices.cs` now exposes:

- `BlueStacksUniversalTuningCandidateBridge UniversalTuningCandidates`;
- `UniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceService UniversalValidatedProfileProvenance`;
- `ResolveCurrentUniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceAsync(Guid profileId, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)`.

The candidate bridge is composed from the existing shared `AutoTuner + GameAdapters`. The provenance service is composed from the existing shared `Profiles + History + UniversalTuningCandidates`.

Construction remains side-effect free for this seam. No candidate generation, profile provenance resolution or extra game discovery is performed merely by constructing `AppServices`, and `InitializeAsync()` does not invoke the new provenance path.

The on-demand method:

1. loads persisted profiles only when called;
2. requires exactly one requested persisted profile;
3. gates to `ProfileKind.Custom + EvidenceLevel.Validated`, non-null `SourceComparisonId`, and non-empty instance name;
4. captures the current environment only after those gates pass;
5. requires exactly one current BlueStacks instance matching the persisted instance name;
6. captures current settings only through the existing BlueStacks allow-list;
7. requires a non-empty allow-list result;
8. delegates final correlation/provenance authority to `UniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceService.ResolveCurrentAsync(...)`;
9. fails closed to `null` on supported profile/history/config I/O, permission, JSON, invalid-data and argument errors.

No fallback to another profile/instance/workload exists.

## Permanent tests

`tests/FFPerformanceEngine.App.SelfTest/Program.cs` now verifies that:

- `AppServices` composes the shared candidate bridge;
- `AppServices` composes the shared persisted-Custom provenance resolver;
- resolving a random unknown profile id returns `null` without manufacturing identity/provenance or requiring unrelated discovery.

All existing Track 4 application workload-routing tests remain intact and GREEN.

