## Authority preserved

- `Observed != Validated` remains unchanged.
- Stable GameId identity remains source-native; no PID/path/display-name inference was added.
- Candidate search support remains exploration/correlation only.
- `UniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceService` remains downstream of specialized persisted validation authority.
- `ProfileService`, `HistoryService`, `ProfileChallengeService`, challenge freshness/evaluator/winner logic, Global Controlled Benchmark Lease, rollback/History and typed PresentMon authority are unchanged.
- No profile creation, validation, winner selection, recommendation, mutation or persistence authority was added.
- No game discovery was added to `InitializeAsync()`.

## Next bounded increment

Proceed to the **Profiles presentation seam** only after this checkpoint's docs-only HEAD passes the full Windows CI.

The next WPF increment must consume only `AppServices.ResolveCurrentUniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceAsync(...)` and present stable GameId, AdapterId and exact candidate values when a real projection exists. It must not reload History independently, rebuild candidate spaces, infer original Auto Tuner mode/identity, rerun validation, select winners or persist universal metadata. `null` means no universal provenance presentation.
